From 05a0b92a71f093cafd98bea11d2e5ad891416537 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 00:10:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 143/257] perf(cpu): execute AVX-512 layout ops natively
 (b6-layout-native)

Add a PXLD-v2 descriptor-driven native plane for reshape/view/contiguous/transpose/slice plus split/concat on the AVX-512 backend, mirroring the verified SVE256 semantics. The native contract predicate is shared by artifact metadata and the runtime dispatch, so a declared kernel is the executed kernel; unsupported dtypes stay on host_reference with an explicit metadata reason. f32/bf16 lanes reproduce the host reference's Python-float round trip (including signaling-NaN quieting) so native outputs are byte-identical to the host_reference baseline. Zero-copy view aliasing is stat-only and remains disabled. Bump artifact payload 6->7 and the native ABI marker to :8.
